    {
        "content": "<p>yeah I think we should be running these - can you open an issue with type=bug?</p>",
        "id": 615594641,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1786358730
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>On a related topic, it would be great to support nested <code>expect</code> statements:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"roc\"><pre><span></span><code>expect {\n  a = 2\n  expect a * 3 == 6\n  b = a + 3\n  expect b == 5\n  c = b * 3\n  c == 15\n}\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I've run into these in Exercism exercises where we have a data structure, we run a sequence of modifications, and we want to test the intermediate states. Of course we could separate each test, but it would be much more verbose and really wouldn't make things much cleaner, probably the opposite. The way I worked around that is by implementing an <code>expect_equal</code> function and calling something like <code>expect_equal(a * 3, 6)?</code>. It works but it looks weird.</p>\n<p>Oh it looks like we've <a href=\"#narrow/channel/304641-ideas/topic/Nested.20expect.20statements/with/475186236\">discussed this before</a>.</p>",
        "id": 615597595,
        "sender_full_name": "Aurélien Geron",
        "timestamp": 1786359838
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Here's the issue, I couldn't tag it as a bug though: <a href=\"https://github.com/roc-lang/roc/issues/10730\">https://github.com/roc-lang/roc/issues/10730</a></p>",
        "id": 615786074,
